<title>USA: Centennial ex-CEO Pinez arraigned.</title>
<headline>Centennial ex-CEO Pinez arraigned.</headline>
<dateline>BOSTON 1997-02-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The former chief executive of Centennial Technologies Inc, Manual Pinez, was arraigned in U.S. District Court here on Friday, according to the U.S. Attorney's office.</p>
<p>Pinez was arrested last night, according to the U.S. Attorney.</p>
<p>Other details, including the charges against Pinez, were not immediately known.</p>
<p>Company officials were not immediately available for comment.  </p>
<p>On Tuesday, Centennial said it fired Pinez, removed its chief financial officer, James Murphy, and announced it launched an inquiry into the accuracy of its most recently reported earnings and prior financial statements.</p>
<p>Centennial shares ended the day on February 10 at 16-3/8 on the New York Stock Exchange, and has not reopened for trading.</p>
</text>
